				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5279</guid>
				<title>SCP-5279</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5279</link>
				<description>

&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: right;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item #:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5279&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Object Class:&lt;/strong&gt; Safe&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Containment Procedures:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5279-1 is placed on a 4 meter high slab of concrete and kept there for 24 hours a day, 4 days a week with exceptions of testing from Level 2 and above research personnel whenever that might occur. It’s also noted that any persons that come into contact with SCP-5279-1 and SCP-5279-2 shouldn’t be wearing green, black, or anything shiny like a ring as wearing such could effect standard testing procedure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Description:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5279-1 is a small seemingly indestructible cardboard box that houses SCP-5279-2, testing shows it’s resistant to fire, gunfire, blunt force, high caliber explosions, and even being doused in lava. Besides SCP-5279-1’s inability to be destroyed or even damaged, the box appears to have no other unusual effects and simply acts as a casing for SCP-5279-2.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SCP-5279-2 is a small black spherical rubber ball with the logo “Coca-Cola” branded on the front, upon research of the ball it was discovered that the company Coca-Cola had never actually made a rubber ball product before and that it was hand crafted.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SCP-5279-2 can be destroyed and damaged, however 24 hours after it’s originally damaged will seemingly regenerate in SCP-5279-1 even if totally obliterated.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While SCP-5279-2 is black in a dormant state, it will start flashing the colors of the rainbow once something black, green, or shiny enters 2 feet within the radius of SCP-5279-2 or SCP-5279-1, this will now be referenced as a “trigger event”.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Exactly 3 minutes and 47 seconds after a trigger event occurs 1-2 people within a mile radius of SCP-5279-2 will instantly die of either heart attack or extreme malnutrition, then SCP-5279-2 will revert back to a black color.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If there are no persons present after 3 minutes and 47 seconds into the trigger event, then SCP-5279-2 will go back to a dormant state and revert back to being black.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;by &lt;span class=&quot;printuser avatarhover&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/viralpepsi&quot;  &gt;&lt;img class=&quot;small&quot; src=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7184083&amp;amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;amp;timestamp=1609559506&quot; alt=&quot;Viralpepsi&quot; style=&quot;background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7184083)&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/viralpepsi&quot;  &gt;Viralpepsi&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 01 Jan 2021 09:11:55 +0000</pubDate>
												<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <p><strong>Item #:</strong> SCP-5279</p> <p><strong>Object Class:</strong> Safe</p> <p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> SCP-5279-1 is placed on a 4 meter high slab of concrete and kept there for 24 hours a day, 4 days a week with exceptions of testing from Level 2 and above research personnel whenever that might occur. It’s also noted that any persons that come into contact with SCP-5279-1 and SCP-5279-2 shouldn’t be wearing green, black, or anything shiny like a ring as wearing such could effect standard testing procedure.</p> <p><strong>Description:</strong> SCP-5279-1 is a small seemingly indestructible cardboard box that houses SCP-5279-2, testing shows it’s resistant to fire, gunfire, blunt force, high caliber explosions, and even being doused in lava. Besides SCP-5279-1’s inability to be destroyed or even damaged, the box appears to have no other unusual effects and simply acts as a casing for SCP-5279-2.</p> <p>SCP-5279-2 is a small black spherical rubber ball with the logo “Coca-Cola” branded on the front, upon research of the ball it was discovered that the company Coca-Cola had never actually made a rubber ball product before and that it was hand crafted.</p> <p>SCP-5279-2 can be destroyed and damaged, however 24 hours after it’s originally damaged will seemingly regenerate in SCP-5279-1 even if totally obliterated.</p> <p>While SCP-5279-2 is black in a dormant state, it will start flashing the colors of the rainbow once something black, green, or shiny enters 2 feet within the radius of SCP-5279-2 or SCP-5279-1, this will now be referenced as a “trigger event”.</p> <p>Exactly 3 minutes and 47 seconds after a trigger event occurs 1-2 people within a mile radius of SCP-5279-2 will instantly die of either heart attack or extreme malnutrition, then SCP-5279-2 will revert back to a black color.</p> <p>If there are no persons present after 3 minutes and 47 seconds into the trigger event, then SCP-5279-2 will go back to a dormant state and revert back to being black.</p> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/viralpepsi" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7184083&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609559506" alt="Viralpepsi" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7184083)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/viralpepsi" >Viralpepsi</a></span></p> 
